{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-instanton-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:instanton-intro","kind":"prose","text":"instanton-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:instanton-intro\"></a><p>The gauge term of the canonical action takes its extremal value when the curvature is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star_q</code>-self-dual. This section defines the categorical instanton and reads off its consequences for the categorical Lagrangian on-shell.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/instanton-intro.md","heading":"","page":"b/sec-instanton-intro","qa":{"counts":{"pass":56,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":19,"unknown":0,"stale":59},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
